{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-83618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ as shown in the table below, compute $a+b+c.$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.1$ | $a$ | $0.5$ | $b$ | $c$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =F(1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =F(3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2+0.2+0.4 \\\\  & =0.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $c,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =F(4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2+0.2+0.4+0.1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.3+0.9+1=2.2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-83618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.7"] ["math" "1.0"] ["math" "1.5"] ["math" "1.8"] ["math" "2.2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83618" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-275826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For a discrete random variable $Y,$ the probability mass function $f(y)$ and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ are shown in the table below. Fill in the blanks.\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.10$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.20$ | $0.15$ |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.10$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-275826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $F(2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(3),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25+0.30 \\\\  & =0.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(4),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(4) & =P(Y\\le 4) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =0.10+0.25+0.30+0.20 \\\\  & =0.85.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-275826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-275826" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-275826" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.35"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-275826" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-275826" "field" "field