Y\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=0)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.20+0.25 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-335957" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335957" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.45"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ (as shown in the table below) and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$, compute $F(2)-F(1).$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.343$ | $0.441$ | $0.189$ | $0.027$ |\n\n$F(2)-F(1)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $F(1)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(Y\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =0.343+0.441 \\\\  & =0.784.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(2)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.343+0.441+0.189 \\\\  & =0.973.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nF(2)-F(1)=0.973-0.784=0.189\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-335964" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335964" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.189"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=6).$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{8}$ | $1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,2,4,6}) \\\\  & =P(X=0)+P(X=2)+P(X=4)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {0,2,4})+P(X=6) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=6) & =F(6)-F(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-83902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{16}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/D