 \\\\  & =P(X\\in {-1,0,1,2}) \\\\  & =P(X=-1)+P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {-1,0,1})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.60-0.35 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335992" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-335992" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335992" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.25"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=5).$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.20$ | $0.45$ | $0.70$ | $0.90$ | $1.00$ |\n\n$P(X=5)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {2,3,4,5}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {2,3,4})+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(X=5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =F(5)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.90-0.70 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-335993" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-335993" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}).$\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $Y$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<Y\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $a\\le Y\\le b,$ not $a<Y\\le b.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}$ to the form $a<Y\\le b.$ Looking at the given possible values of $Y,$ we see that $\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y$ is equivalent to $0<Y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{2}\\le Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}) & =P(0<Y\\le \\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =F(\\frac{3}{2})-F(0) \\\\  & =0.8-0.1 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-83623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1