n possible values of $Y,$ we see that $Y<\\frac{5}{2}$ is equivalent to $Y\\le 2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<\\frac{5}{2}) & =P(1<Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.7-0.3 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-83912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.2"] ["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.4"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-336006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(1<X\\le 3).$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{7}{20}$ | $\\frac{11}{20}$ | $\\frac{17}{20}$ | $1$ |\n\n$P(1<X\\le 3)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-336006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $X$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 3) & =F(3)-F(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{20}-\\frac{7}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-336006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-336006" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-336006" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/q