"q-83622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.4"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.6"] ["math" "0.7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-124948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(-1.5<X\\le 0.5).$\n\n| $x$ | $-1.5$ | $-1$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ | $\\frac{13}{16}$ | $1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-124948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $X$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.5<X\\le 0.5) & =F(0.5)-F(-1.5) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-124948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-124948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-124948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{16}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-124948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-125069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X\\ge 6).$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-125069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(X\\ge 6).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $X\\ge 6,$ not $X>6.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $X\\ge 6$ to the form $X>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $X,$ we see that $X\\ge 6$ is equivalent to $X>4.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6) & =P(X>4) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.3 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-125069" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-125069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-125069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.2"] ["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.4"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-125069" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-124953" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X\\ge 5.5).$\n\n| $x$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ | $3.5$ | $4.5$ | $5.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ | $1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-124953" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(X\\ge 5.5).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $X\\ge 5.5,$ not $X>5.5.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $X\\ge 5.5$ to the form $X>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $X,$ we see that $X\\ge 5.5$ is equivalent to $X>4.5.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5.5) & =P(X>4.5) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4.5) \\\\  & =1-F(4.5) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-124953" "field