lution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>4) & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.3 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83803" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-83803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.4"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.6"] ["math" "0.7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83803" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $T$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(t)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(T\\ge 6).$\n\n| $t$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(t)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $T$ is a function $F(t)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(t)=P(T\\le t).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(T>a)=1-P(T\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(T\\ge 6).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $T\\ge 6,$ not $T>6.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $T\\ge 6$ to the form $T>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $T,$ we see that $T\\ge 6$ is equivalent to $T>3.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T\\ge 6) & =P(T>3) \\\\  & =1-P(T\\le 3) \\\\  & =1-F(3) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-83921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $T$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(t)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(T\\ge 2).$\n\n| $t$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(t)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{6}$ | $1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $T$ is a function $F(t)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(t)=P(T\\le t).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(T>a)=1-P(T\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(T\\ge 2).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $T\\ge 2,$ not $T>2.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $T\\ge 2$ to the form $T>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $T,$ we see that $T\\ge 2$ is equivalent to $T>\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T\\ge 2) & =P(T>\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =1-P(T\\le \\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =1-F(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83922" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "43b14bad1253e5070796bc3484f70298a2ebad6dfb04f6f89ce28f1e905ec5b2"} {"question" "q-83922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "q-83922" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/state.json" "file_sha256" "e084da2a61ea0b0fafc742c6dffe6c76ab47768695aa82466ee6384e254cddbf"} {"question" "e-7379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y),$ shown in the table below, and the cumulative distribution function $F(y),$ compute $F(2).$\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/example-7379.json" "file_sha256" "606a4147ba8a659dc4e449e0df9d06d4ef7252ae86abb95bde35ff78c9cb0eb4"} {"question" "e-7379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is the function $F(y)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(y) = P(Y \\leq y).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/example-7379.json" "file_sha256" "606a4147ba8a659dc4e449e0df9d06d4ef7252ae86abb95bde35ff78c9cb0eb4"} {"question" "e-7382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=5).$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ | $0.50$ | $0.90$ | $1.0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/example-7382.json" "file_sha256" "e9e745cc5d262ac52487e04e528532fadeddee335b9fe2afa81a1637a48050bf"} {"question" "e-7382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {1,3,5}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=3)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in {1,3})+P(X=5) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =F(3)+P(X=5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =F(5)-F(3) \\\\  & =0.50-0.45 \\\\  & =0.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/example-7382.json" "file_sha256" "e9e745cc5d262ac52487e04e528532fadeddee335b9fe2afa81a1637a48050bf"} {"question" "e-7381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ shown in the table below, compute $P\\left( 2 \\leq  Y <     5 \\right).$\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ | $1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/example-7381.json" "file_sha256" "fcbee8634b72fdfea9fb880a2e74e823c218534f7321783ac9475e432ae591be"} {"question" "e-7381" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is the function $F(y)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(y) = P(Y \\leq y).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $Y$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a <            X \\leq b) = F(b) - F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P\\left( 2 \\leq  Y <     5 \\right).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $a \\leq  Y <    b,$ not $a <           Y \\leq b.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $2 \\leq  Y <     5$ to the form $a <         X \\leq b.$ Looking at the given possible values of $Y,$ we see that $2 \\leq Y$ is equivalent to $1 <        Y,$ and  $Y<   5$ is equivalent to $Y \\leq 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le Y<5) & =P(1<Y\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(4)-F(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/example-7381.json" "file_sha256" "fcbee8634b72fdfea9fb880a2e74e823c218534f7321783ac9475e432ae591be"} {"question" "e-7414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X \\gt 2).$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ | $0.8$ | $0.9$ | $1.0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/example-7414.json" "file_sha256" "407b4e3594c3f544a462ebabe94100c323531ed9bdb1fc8e5e781288fa59d389"} {"question" "e-7414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>2) & =1-P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =1-F(2) \\\\  & =1-0.6 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069335/example-7414.json" "file_sha256" "407b4e3594c3f544a462ebabe94100c323531ed9bdb1fc8e5e781288fa59d389"}] "usage" {"e-7381" [] "e-7379" [] "e-7382" [] "q-83618" [] "q-83803" [] "q-83622" [] "q-83623" [] "e-7414" []} "basis" 2364 "retractions" [[17592186129816 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nGiven that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$ and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ as shown in the table below, compute $a + b + c$.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.1$ | $a$ | $0.5$ | $b$ | $c$ |"] [17592186129821 :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(\\frac{1}{2} \\le Y \\le \\frac{3}{2})$.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |"] [17592186129820 :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(4 < X \\le 6)$.\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $0.9$ | $1.0$ |"] [17592186129822 :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X > 4)$.\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | $0.8$ | $1.0$ |"] [17592186128954 :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function $f(y)$, shown in the table below, and the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$, compute $F(2)$.\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ |"] [17592186128954 :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is the function $F(y)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(y) = P(Y \\leq y)\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(2) &= P(Y \\le 2) \\\\\n&= P(Y ∈ {1, 2}) \\\\\n&= P(Y = 1) + P(Y = 2) \\\\\n&= f(1) + f(2) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{8} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128956 :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X=5)$.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ | $9$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ | $0.50$ | $0.90$ | $1.0$ |"] [17592186128956 :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(5) &= P(X \\le 5) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {1, 3, 5}) \\\\\n&= P(X = 1) + P(X = 3) + P(X = 5) \\\\\n&= P(X ∈ {1, 3}) + P(X = 5) \\\\\n&= P(X \\le 3) + P(X = 5) \\\\\n&= F(3) + P(X = 5)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X = 5) &= F(5) - F(3) \\\\\n&= 0.50 - 0.45 \\\\\n&= 0.05\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128955 :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $Y$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(y)$ shown in the table below, compute $P\\left(2 \\leq Y < 5 \\right)$.\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(y)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{6}$ | $1$ |"] [17592186128955 :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is the function $F(y)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(y) = P(Y \\leq y)\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $Y$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a < X \\leq b) = F(b) - F(a)\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute\n\n$$\nP\\left(2 \\leq Y < 5 \\right)\n$$\n\nHowever, this interval is stated in the form\n\n$$\na \\leq Y < b\n$$\n\nnot\n\n$$\na < Y \\leq b\n$$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval\n\n$$\n2 \\leq Y < 5\n$$\n\nto the form\n\n$$\na < X \\leq b\n$$\n\nLooking at the given possible values of $Y$, we see that\n\n$$\n2 \\leq Y\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $1 < Y$, and $Y< 5$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\nY \\leq 4\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(2 \\le Y < 5) &= P(1 < Y \\le 4) \\\\\n&= F(4) - F(1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128957 :question/problem "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X \\gt 2)$.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $F(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ | $0.8$ | $0.9$ | $1.0$ |"] [17592186128957 :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x)\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X > a) = 1 - P(X\\leq a) = 1-F(a)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X > 2) &= 1 - P(X \\le 2) \\\\\n&= 1 - F(2) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0.6 \\\\\n&= 0.4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186128691 17592186128692 17592186128693 17592186128694 17592186128695 17592186128715 17592186128716 17592186128717 17592186128718 17592186128719 17592186128721 17592186128722 17592186128723 17592186128724 17592186128725 17592186128727 17592186128728 17592186128729 17592186128730 17592186128731] "immutable_fields" [[17592186128690 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128690 :answer-field/id] [17592186128690 :answer-field/key] [17592186128690 :answer-field/type] [17592186128714 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128714 :answer-field/id] [17592186128714 :answer-field/key] [17592186128714 :answer-field/type] [17592186128720 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128720 :answer-field/id] [17592186128720 :answer-field/key] [17592186128720 :answer-field/type] [17592186128726 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128726 :answer-field/id] [17592186128726 :answer-field/key] [17592186128726 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
